.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tix-repo-add 1  "add " 
.SH NAME
tix\-repo\-add \- Register a repository in config (without cloning)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtix repo add\fR [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-alias\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-O\fR|\fB\-\-owner\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-level\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIREPO\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Register a repository in config (without cloning)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-alias\fR \fI<ALIAS>\fR
Alias to register under (defaults to the repository name)
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to the global config file (overrides TIX_CONFIG_PATH and the platform default)
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Output format for commands that support it (also forwarded to plugins as \-\-tix\-output)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
toml
.IP \(bu 2
default
.RE
.TP
\fB\-O\fR, \fB\-\-owner\fR \fI<OWNER>\fR
Owner for a bare `repo` argument (beats `[defaults].default_repository_owner`)
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fI<LOG_LEVEL>\fR
Set the log level (trace, debug, info, warn, error)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Set the log level to trace (shorthand for \-\-log\-level trace)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Set the log level to warn (shorthand for \-\-log\-level warn)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIREPO\fR>
Full URL, `owner/repo`, or bare `repo`
